<BaseLayout title="Sources and rights"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Provenance, access & permissions</p><h1>Open about<br/><em>our sources.</em></h1></header><div class="prose"><h2>Official award facts</h2><p>The <a href="https://www.nobelprize.org/organization/developer-zone-2/">Nobel Prize API</a> supplies the catalogue. Saved responses and import dates make it possible to reproduce the public facts. Official motivations are attributed on award pages. We link to complete official pages rather than mirroring their explanatory texts or media.</p><h2>Our explanations</h2><p>Original site-written explanations are offered under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. PDF and EPUB overviews are built from the same Markdown and bibliography as the web article. A download appears only when the exact artifact has passed integrity validation. Draft exports are identified as unreviewed inside the documents.</p><h2>Original research is a separate category</h2><p>“Read original at source” opens a verified publisher or repository landing page. It does not promise a free PDF. A publisher version, accepted manuscript, working paper and preprint can have different rights. Access conditions are recorded per version.</p><p>We default to external links. Locally hosted originals require explicit permission evidence, a named verifier, a verification date, and a checksum. EPUB conversions additionally require verified conversion permission and quality review. A free-to-read page, an open-access label, or a guessed PDF URL is insufficient.</p><h2>Portraits and typefaces</h2><p>Portrait monograms are used until an individual image’s source, photographer, license and permitted display have been verified. No Nobel-hosted portraits are hotlinked. STIX Two Text is bundled locally under the SIL Open Font License; KaTeX and its fonts are distributed under their packaged licenses. License texts are retained in the repository.</p><h2>No unauthorized mirrors</h2><p>We do not bypass paywalls or DRM, reproduce copyrighted books, or generate EPUBs from scans with uncertain rights. Personal research copies must remain outside the public repository and site build. A missing original format is reported plainly.</p><h2>Corrections and takedowns</h2><p>Please <a href="https://github.com/willtheorangeguy/econ-nobel/issues">open an issue</a> identifying the exact source or asset, the concern, and supporting evidence. Disputed permissions should be resolved before an asset is published.</p></div></BaseLayout>
